---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, href } from '../data/site';
import { decomposition, measurements, fine } from '../data/measurements';
import FormatFlow from '../components/charts/FormatFlow.astro';
import DecompositionFigure from '../components/charts/DecompositionFigure.astro';

const formats = [
  { name: 'PACE JSONL', origin: 'the SDK’s own writer', split: 'full three-way split' },
  { name: 'Chrome Trace Event', origin: 'the standard trace format', split: 'dur only, no split' },
  { name: 'perf sched timehist', origin: 'perf’s scheduling analysis', split: 'derived, not measured' },
  { name: 'perf trace', origin: 'perf’s event trace', split: 'dur only, no split' },
];

const codes = [
  ['io-error', 'the trace could not be read'],
  ['parse-error', 'the trace is malformed where it was read'],
  ['format-unknown', 'no parser recognised the file'],
  ['empty-trace', 'the invariant holds vacuously, so verify fails'],
  ['unsupported-output', 'the requested output format does not exist'],
  ['write-error', 'the report could not be written'],
  ['invalid-argument', 'a flag or a value is not usable'],
];

const api = [
  ['pace_config_init(&cfg)', 'fills a config with the documented defaults; call this before touching any field'],
  ['pace_session_create(&cfg, &session)', 'allocates a session; the only call that allocates'],
  ['pace_session_register_thread(session, &thread)', 'once per thread you intend to sample'],
  ['pace_session_sample(session, thread, &sample)', 'one sample on the calling thread; no allocation'],
  ['pace_session_stats(session, &stats)', 'the tier, thread count, sample count, degraded count and whether the eBPF tier attached'],
  ['pace_session_destroy(session)', 'invalidates every thread handle'],
];
---

<Base
  title="Docs — PACE"
  description="The trace formats PACE reads, the C API, the CLI, the error codes, and the invariant the analyzer enforces."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="section-label">Documentation</div>
      <h1>The reference, in one place</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Everything here is derived from the repository at
        {' '}<span class="mono">{site.repo.replace('https://github.com/', '')}</span>. Where a figure
        appears, it is generated from a committed measurement artifact at build time.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn" href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/pace-sdk/docs/INTEGRATION.md`}>
          <i class="ph ph-book"></i>
          Integration guide
        </a>
        <a class="btn" href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/pace-sdk/docs/ACCURACY.md`}>
          <i class="ph ph-ruler"></i>
          Accuracy method
        </a>
        <a class="btn" href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/pace-analyzer/README.md`}>
          <i class="ph ph-terminal-window"></i>
          Analyzer README
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-label">The invariant</div>
      <h2>What every consumer can rely on</h2>
      <DecompositionFigure />
      <p>
        Two functions enforce it, and they are the two a consumer should gate on:
        {' '}<span class="mono">pace verify</span> at the command line, which exits non-zero when a
        trace breaks the rule, and the analyzer's own check as it reads, which refuses to report a
        trace it could not verify.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-label">Formats</div>
      <h2>What the analyzer reads, and what each format can support</h2>
      <FormatFlow />
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Format</th>
              <th>Where it comes from</th>
              <th>What it can carry</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              formats.map((f) => (
                <tr>
                  <td>{f.name}</td>
                  <td class="dim">{f.origin}</td>
                  <td class={f.split.startsWith('full') ? 'ok' : 'dim'}>{f.split}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="callout">
        <div class="callout-title">A format with no split is reported as having none</div>
        <p>
          A plain Chrome trace gives the analyzer a duration and nothing else. It prints a dash where
          the preempted and blocked figures would go, draws an empty bar, and raises no findings
          against that thread. The analyzer also counts and skips malformed lines rather than failing
          the whole parse, and reports the count it skipped.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-label">C API</div>
      <h2>The calls, in the order you make them</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Call</th>
              <th>What it does</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              api.map(([call, what]) => (
                <tr>
                  <td><span class="mono">{call}</span></td>
                  <td class="dim" style="white-space:normal">{what}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="panel">
          <h3><i class="ph ph-users"></i> The threading contract</h3>
          <p>
            The public header states which calls are thread-safe, that an observer must not re-enter
            the session, and that <span class="mono">destroy</span> invalidates every thread handle.
            Read it before you call any of this from more than one place.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3><i class="ph ph-flag"></i> Saying "unknown" instead of zero</h3>
          <p>
            A sample carries a <span class="mono">struct_size</span> and flags
            {' '}<span class="mono">PACE_SAMPLE_F_HAS_PREEMPTED</span> and
            {' '}<span class="mono">PACE_SAMPLE_F_HAS_BLOCKED</span>, so the API can report "this
            platform cannot tell you" rather than a zero that looks like a measurement.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-label">Analyzer</div>
      <h2>The commands and their exit codes</h2>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="panel">
          <h3><i class="ph ph-terminal-window"></i> Commands</h3>
          <pre><code>{`pace analyze <trace> [--output report.html]
pace inspect <trace>
pace verify <trace>
pace convert <in> --to pace|chrome`}</code></pre>
          <p>
            <span class="mono">analyze</span> and <span class="mono">verify</span> read the trace line
            by line, so memory is proportional to the thread count rather than the sample count.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3><i class="ph ph-warning-octagon"></i> Error codes</h3>
          <div class="table-scroll">
            <table>
              <tbody>
                {
                  codes.map(([code, what]) => (
                    <tr>
                      <td><span class="mono">{code}</span></td>
                      <td class="dim" style="white-space:normal">{what}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))
                }
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-label">Accuracy</div>
      <h2>Every measurement the harness makes, and what it is gated on</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Measurement</th>
              <th>n</th>
              <th>Median</th>
              <th>p95</th>
              <th>Gate</th>
              <th></th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              measurements.map((m) => (
                <tr>
                  <td>{m.short}</td>
                  <td class="dim">{m.n}</td>
                  <td>{fine(m.median)}</td>
                  <td>{fine(m.p95)}</td>
                  <td class="dim">{fine(m.threshold)}</td>
                  <td class={m.skipped ? 'dim' : m.passed ? 'ok' : 'bad'}>
                    {m.skipped ? 'reported' : m.passed ? 'pass' : 'fail'}
                  </td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
            <tr>
              <td>decomposition balance</td>
              <td class="dim">{decomposition.samples.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
              <td>0.0000 %</td>
              <td>0.0000 %</td>
              <td class="dim">0.0100 %</td>
              <td class="ok">pass</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Median and p95 are relative errors against a source that does not come from PACE, and the
        gate is the threshold this repository fails a build on. The full method, the environment
        artifact and the raw per-run records are in
        {' '}<a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/pace-sdk/results/accuracy.json`}>the committed
        artifact</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-label">Also on this site</div>
      <h2>Where to go next</h2>
      <div class="card-row">
        <div class="panel">
          <h3><i class="ph ph-download-simple"></i> Install</h3>
          <p>Packages, the toolchain, and the three things that go wrong.</p>
          <p><a href={href('install/')}>Install it</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3><i class="ph ph-activity"></i> The hosted service</h3>
          <p>The same analyzer over HTTP, so you can skip the build.</p>
          <p><a href={href('service/')}>See the API</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3><i class="ph ph-flask"></i> Research</h3>
          <p>The method, the evidence, and where the claim stops.</p>
          <p><a href={href('research/')}>Read the research</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
